  "narrative": {
    "intro": "HUBZone set-aside obligations are $415M in FY2026 to date. The program recorded 1,210 awards with an average award size of $343K. Obligations fell 54.9% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows higher totals in prior years: FY21 was $938M, FY22 was $1B, FY23 was $1.1B, FY24 was $1B, and FY25 was $920M. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer in FY2026 to date, obligating $144M, followed by the Department of Homeland Security with $72.8M and the Department of Labor with $51.3M. Other top buyers include the Department of Transportation, Department of Health and Human Services, and Department of State. Other Computer Related Services is the largest industry by obligations at $113M, followed by Other Technical and Trade Schools at $41.6M and Facilities Support Services at $38.6M. The largest vendors in FY2026 to date include T&H SERVICES, LLC with $22.8M and PANAMERICA COMPUTERS, INC. with $19.2M. All figures are contract obligations and FY2026 totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
