        "heading": "Which agencies are driving FY2026 HUBZone obligations?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $144M in FY2026 to date. The Department of Homeland Security follows with $72.8M and the Department of Labor with $51.3M. Additional buyers with notable obligations include the Department of Transportation at $30.6M and the Department of Health and Human Services at $26.1M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are HUBZone awards by vendor and industry?",
        "body": "Other Computer Related Services is the largest industry, with $113M in FY2026 to date, followed by Other Technical and Trade Schools at $41.6M and Facilities Support Services at $38.6M. T&H SERVICES, LLC is the single largest vendor at $22.8M, with PANAMERICA COMPUTERS, INC. and FEDERAL RESOURCES CORPORATION next at $19.2M and $17.2M respectively. The program recorded 1,210 awards, producing an average award size of $343K."
      }
